1. ACCEPTANCE OF TERMS

By downloading, installing or using TEMPOX: Brain & Reflex, you declare that you have read and agree to these Terms of Service and our Privacy Policy. If you do not agree, do not use the app.

2. CONDITIONS OF USE

- The game is intended for personal, non-commercial entertainment;
- Reverse engineering, modifying, decompiling or distributing altered versions of the app is forbidden;
- Automated methods to manipulate scores, coins or achievements are forbidden;
- Misuse that harms other users experience or Google Play services may result in suspension of access to online features.

3. INTELLECTUAL PROPERTY

All rights over the source code, game mechanics, graphic art, sounds, visual identity and the TEMPOX brand belong to Elias Chanisso / Biz-Flow, protected by Brazilian and international intellectual property law. These terms grant only a limited, revocable and non-exclusive license for personal use of the app.

4. IN-APP PURCHASES

- Virtual products (such as permanent ad removal) are purchased exclusively through the Google Play Store, which processes payment;
- The ad removal purchase is tied to your Google Account and can be restored inside the app via Restore purchases;
- Refunds follow the Google Play Store policies; requests may also be filed through our support;
- Coins and progression items are fictional, have no real monetary value, are non-convertible and non-transferable between accounts.

5. LIMITATION OF LIABILITY AND WARRANTIES

TEMPOX is provided as is. We do not guarantee uninterrupted or error-free operation on every device and Android version. To the extent permitted by law, the developer is not liable for:

- Loss of local progress due to reinstalling, changing devices or clearing system data;
- Temporary unavailability of features that depend on third-party services (ads, payments);
- Indirect damages arising from app usage.

6. CHANGES AND TERMINATION

These terms may be updated to reflect new features or legal requirements; the current version will always be available with an updated date. The developer may discontinue the service, keeping the right of use of installed versions.

